zsh-wasm — License
==================

zsh-wasm is distributed under the Zsh license.

This file covers **zsh-wasm's own code**: the build scripts in `bin/`, the
JavaScript runtime in `web/` (`zsh-runtime.js`, `zsh-worker.js`, `zsh-loader.js`,
`index.html`, `test.html`), the npm package metadata in `npm/`, the embedding
glue written for this project (`embed/`, the `*_mod.c`, `*_embed.[ch]` and
`*.mdd` files under `awk-src/`, `sed-src/`, `bc-src/`, `sbase-src/` and
`diff-src/`), and the documentation.

zsh-wasm also **bundles six third-party codebases**, compiled together into the
single `zsh.wasm` binary this project publishes. They are all permissively
licensed, but they are not all under this license, and two of them carry terms
about the use of a name in advertising.

**Those texts are in `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md`, and they travel with the
binary.** Redistributing `zsh.wasm` — or the npm package, or a bundle built from
it — means redistributing all six, and that file carries the notices they
require. Ship it alongside.


